Use the POSIX field name for the statvfs flags on zedBSD

Path.inc picks <sys/statvfs.h> and struct statvfs for every system that is
not Linux, FreeBSD, AIX or managarm, and zedBSD is one of those.  It then
reads the flags field under the name struct statfs gives it, f_flags,
because the list of systems that use the POSIX name names only four.

struct statvfs has f_flag.  A system that gets the POSIX struct and the BSD
field name cannot compile this file, so zedBSD is added to the list rather
than growing a second name for one field in its own headers.

This is not specific to zedBSD: any system reaching the statvfs branch and
not named on line 113 has the same problem.

--- a/llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc
+++ b/llvm/lib/Support/Unix/Path.inc
@@ -111,7 +111,7 @@
 #endif
 
 #if defined(__NetBSD__) || defined(__DragonFly__) || defined(__GNU__) ||       \
-    defined(__MVS__)
+    defined(__MVS__) || defined(__ZEDBSD__)
 #define STATVFS_F_FLAG(vfs) (vfs).f_flag
 #else
 #define STATVFS_F_FLAG(vfs) (vfs).f_flags
